The studies HRP-301 (VERDANT-1), HRP-201 and GLV-12-301, the products lumiravostat (Ostrevia)
and GLV-12, the sponsors, sites, participants and all identifiers are fictional. Regulations,
guidelines and standards (ICH E6(R3), 21 CFR 50, Regulation (EU) No 536/2014, the New Drugs and
Clinical Trials Rules 2019, ISO 24495-1) are named for education; the app summarises them and
does not reproduce their text, and nothing in it is regulatory or legal advice. The jargon
dictionary was written for this app and is not taken from any published word list. Readability
formulas are public formulas; the New Dale-Chall word list is not included.

The app is not a validated system and must not hold real participant data. Everything stays in
the browser; there is no AI service: all scoring is by rules.

src/shared/consent.ts and src/shared/jargon.ts are shared with the Protocol Builder
(https://github.com/randomthingsonlineatsk-cloud/protocol-builder), by the same author and under
the same licence.
